# data-storage runtime data — DO NOT DELETE

The following paths contain **production/runtime data** and must **never** be deleted,
truncated, moved, or `rm -rf` by agents, cleanup scripts, or git operations:

- `data-storage/corpus/` — derived datasets, parquet, offline episodes
- `data-storage/pipeline/` — pipeline intermediate outputs
- `data-storage/lerobot-qc/` — QC cache, sidecar, delivery videos
- `data-storage/stream/` — hot-tier stream ingest data
- `data-storage/ego-archive/` — cold archive
- `data-storage/logs/` — operational logs (safe to rotate, not bulk-delete without user request)
- `data-storage/registry/` — episode registry DB

Allowed maintenance (only when user explicitly requests):

- `ego-cleanup-bak-dirs.sh` — removes only `*.bak` dirs under `data-storage/stream/<station>/`
- `ego-prune-old-images.sh` — prunes Docker **images** only, not data-storage files

When writing cleanup scripts, add explicit guards and never use broad `rm -rf data-storage/`.
